{title: 264 - O for That Flame of Living Fire}
{subtitle: SDA Hymnal #264 • MENDON • 8.8.9.8}
{lyricist: William H. Bathurst}
{composer: German Melody}
{key: Ab}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: Moderato}
{meta: hymn_number 264}
{meta: tune MENDON}
{meta: meter 8.8.9.8}
{meta: category Holy Spirit - }

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[Ab]Ofor that [Eb]flame [Ab]of [Eb/G]living fire
[Ab]Which shone so [Fm]bright [Bbm]insaints [Ab]of [Eb/G]old;
[Eb/Bb]Which bade their [Fm/C]souls [Ab]to [Db]heaven [Fm/C]aspire,
[Ab]Calm in distress, [Bbm]indanger [Ab]bold!
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[Ab]Where [Eb/G]is [Ab]that [Eb]spirit, Lord, [Ab]which [Eb/Bb]dwelt
[Ab]In Abram's [Fm]breast, [Bbm]and [Ab]sealed Him [Eb/G]Thine?
[Eb/Bb]Which made Paul's [Fm/C]heart [Ab]with [Db]sorrow [Fm/C]melt,
[Ab]And glow with [Fm]energy [Eb/G]divine?
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[Ab]That [Eb/G]spirit which [Ab]from [Eb/G]age [Ab]to [Eb/Bb]age
[Ab]Proclaimed Thy [Fm]love, [Bbm]and [Ab]taught Thy [Eb/G]ways?
[Eb/Bb]Brightened Isaiah's [Db]vivid [Fm/C]page,
[Ab]And breathed in [Fm]David's [Ab]hallowed lays?
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
[Ab]Is [Eb/G]not [Ab]Thy [Eb]grace [Ab]as [Eb/G]mighty now
[Ab]As when Elijah felt its [Eb/G]power?
[Eb/Bb]When glory [Fm/C]beamed [Ab]from [Db]Moses' [Fm/C]brow,
[Ab]Or Job endured [Bbm]the [Ab]trying [Eb/G]hour?
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 5}
[Ab]Remember, [Eb]Lord, [Ab]the [Eb/G]ancient days;
[Ab]Renew Thy [Fm]work, [Bbm]Thy [Ab]grace restore;
[Eb/Bb]And while [Fm/C]to [Ab]Thee [Db]our [Eb7]hearts [Fm/C]we [Eb/Bb]raise,
[Ab]On us Thy [Fm]Holy [Ab]Spirit pour.
{end_of_verse}
